      "code": "G",
      "title": "Comparatives and superlatives",
      "rule": "Qiyosiy daraja (\"…roq\"): qisqa sifatlarga *-er* qoʻshiladi va *than* (\"-dan\") ishlatiladi: *Bekzod is taller than Aziz.* Orttirma daraja (\"eng …\"): *the + sifat + -est*: *Hamida is the oldest in the family.* Uzun sifatlar oldiga *more / the most* qoʻyiladi: *more expensive, the most beautiful.* Imlo: *big → bigger → the biggest; happy → happier → the happiest.* Istisnolar: *good → better → the best; bad → worse → the worst.*",
      "examples": [
        "Bekzod is taller than Aziz.",
        "Tashkent is bigger than Jizzax.",
        "Hamida is the oldest in the family.",
        "This bag is more expensive than that bag.",
        "Samarkand is the most beautiful city.",
        "Tea is better than coffee."
      ],
      "words": [
        { "en": "tall", "uz": "baland boʻyli" },
        { "en": "than", "uz": "-dan (koʻra)" },
        { "en": "older", "uz": "kattaroq (yoshi)" },
        { "en": "bigger", "uz": "kattaroq" },
        { "en": "more expensive", "uz": "qimmatroq" },
        { "en": "the most beautiful", "uz": "eng goʻzal" },
        { "en": "better", "uz": "yaxshiroq" },
        { "en": "the best", "uz": "eng yaxshi" }
      ],
      "text": {
        "title": "Our family and our cities",
        "en": "Karim is 55. Nodira is 50. Karim is older than Nodira. But Hamida is the oldest in the family. Bekzod is 17. He is the youngest. He is taller than Dilnoza. Usmat is a small town. Jizzax is bigger than Usmat. Tashkent is the biggest city in Uzbekistan. Samarkand is the most beautiful city. Dilnoza thinks Samarkand is better than Tashkent."
      },
